Q: Unzipping files in Python A: <p>try this:</p>
<pre><code>import zipfile
def un_zipFiles(path):
    files=os.listdir(path)
    for file in files:
        if file.endswith('.zip'):
            filePath=path+'/'+file
            zip_file = zipfile.ZipFile(filePath)
            for names in zip_file.namelist():
                zip_file.extract(names,path)
            zip_file.close() 
</code></pre>
<p>path : unzip file's path</p>

Q: How to import Mockk dependency in Kotlin class A: <p>The issue shown in the screenshot is that the import <strong><code>import io.mockk.every</code></strong> is causing an errorr meaning the <strong>Mockk dependency</strong> is not properly added to your project.</p>
<p>To fix this in a <strong>Kotlin + Spring Boot (Maven)</strong> project, add the following dependency to your <strong><code>pom.xml</code></strong>:</p>
<pre class="lang-xml prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;dependency&gt;
    &lt;groupId&gt;io.mockk&lt;/groupId&gt;
    &lt;artifactId&gt;mockk&lt;/artifactId&gt;
    &lt;version&gt;1.13.10&lt;/version&gt; &lt;!-- or latest version --&gt;
    &lt;scope&gt;test&lt;/scope&gt;
&lt;/dependency&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>If you’re using <strong>Gradle (Kotlin DSL)</strong>, add this instead:</p>
<pre class="lang-bash prettyprint-override"><code>testImplementation(&quot;io.mockk:mockk:1.13.10&quot;)
</code></pre>
<p>Then reload or reimport your project (e.g., <strong><code>mvn clean test</code></strong> or <strong><code>gradle build</code></strong>).<br />
After that, the import should work:</p>
<pre class="lang-xml prettyprint-override"><code>import io.mockk.every
import io.mockk.mockk
</code></pre>
<p>You can then use Mockk in your test class like:</p>
<pre><code>val service = mockk&lt;MyService&gt;()
every { service.doSomething() } returns &quot;mocked result&quot;
</code></pre>
